    {
      "id": "GCR-02",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-gram-column-measures",
      "title": "The measure in a two-stage column integral has n copies of a local Haar modulus",
      "statement": "For a nonnegative measurable test and compatible coordinate Haar measures, the local integral on the block fibre equals c_v(t)^n times the integral on the first-vector fibre of the complement integral. At a field place c_v(t)=|t|_v^{-2}.",
      "hypotheses": "Additive Haar on R and one F-basis of E are used to construct all three measures. The source and target have the same represented first scalar t≠0. Near the centre x=a²t with a(t)=1, and the Schur complement is nonsingular.",
      "correspondence": "For the moving target the weight is κ₁(a) cm(a)^n; at the centre these are 1 and the pushforward modulus of multiplication by t. Uniqueness for regular families upgrades the integrated change of variables to the exact target.",
      "dependencies": [
        "GCR-01",
        "GFG-02"
      ],
      "equations": [
        "lifts-gram-column-stages"
      ],
